   "note": "THE OVERLAY LESSON, RESOLVED RATHER THAN ABANDONED. LEADER dropped its overtone because a second voice mixed DRY is company and not character — it has its own onsets, and the ear localises onsets, so in the intelligibility band it formed words and outside it it droned. OVERLORD's answer was unison. THIS is the third answer and it is the one that makes a TIMBRE: keep OVERLORD's male-to-female ratio (1.00 : 0.62) and put the overlay entirely IN ECHO — no dry signal at all, three taps at 34 ms decaying 0.55 — so every onset it has arrives inside the body's own and it is heard as the voice's tail. A tail is a timbre. Under that sits LEADER OF EARTH itself as the element: the espeak build, band-limited to 110-900 Hz and also in echo, giving the mass the eight accents were always for without letting them speak. HARMONY IS MEASURED, NOT WRITTEN DOWN: the octave is computed from the f0 the two models actually render on this document's own opening, because a number typed here would be wrong by whatever the retune moved, and it would still look deliberate — which is precisely what happened to OVERLORD, whose own note called its interval eleven cents flat when the arithmetic says fifty.",
